#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0132B expect=violation domain=ADLBC
#note "PCHG as the lone gate member AND the lone trigger, over a dataset with NO BASE column at all -- the two halves M2-D24 keeps apart, in one file. PCHG is the only entry of Requirements.Variables.Any [CHG, PCHG, R2BASE] that is declared, so the flat Any is satisfied and the rule executes (spell it All and this REDS as skipped). BASE is ABSENT, so the bare empty(BASE) leaf broadcast-folds TRUE (EC-43) and row 1, whose PCHG is populated, FIRES. ⛔ This is the scenario that proves the constraint: put BASE (or AVAL) into the Requirements facet and this file REDS as skipped -- the rule would stop detecting the very defect it exists for, silently, with every other gate green. Row 2 has PCHG missing -> first conjunct false -> silent. BASE is an absent Output_Variable and is not pinned."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 AVAL=10 PCHG=20
dataset ADLBC structure=BDS
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col PARAMCD type=Char
col AVAL    type=Num
col PCHG    type=Num
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | ALB | 10 | 20
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1023 | ALB | 10 | .
